# SVG Processing Rules

Author: slspencer
Copyright: 2026

## Scope

Applies to all SVG and XML parsing/manipulation.

## Rules

- Do not introduce new regex-based SVG/XML parsing.
- Use parser/DOM-based workflows (`xmltree`, `svg_dom`) only.
- Update the DOM tree directly; avoid brittle string munging.
- Use terminology consistently:
  - **flatten** = bake-in transforms.
  - **interpolation** = convert curves to polylines.
- Prefer deterministic transforms and stable element ordering.

## Safety Checks

- Preserve valid SVG structure after edits.
- Avoid destructive normalization unless explicitly requested.
